, separate answers</h2></div> <div class="section-meta">2 / 8 areas with reported AI use</div> </div> <div class="status-note tone-amber"> <strong>Official AI disclosure</strong><span>The developer has disclosed generative AI use. The original source defines its scope.</span> </div> <p class="section-lede">A Touhou-themed roguelike deckbuilder released on Oct 26, 2026, self-developed and self-published by EskiNott Game Studio and filed under Adventure, Casual, Indie, RPG and Strategy. The Steam AI disclosure states that generative AI was used in the games art production for both image creation and image enhancement, and was used to translate the localised content. This site records art and translation as used on that wording and the remaining six areas as areas the disclosure does not address. Every finding rests on the developer own statement and none of it has been independently audited.</p>  <div class="table-wrap"> <table class="ai-table"> <thead> <tr><th>Area</th><th>Scope</th><th>Status</th><th>Notes</th></tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>In-game generation</strong><small>In-game AI</small></td> <td class="muted">Content generated during play</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Code</strong><small>Code</small></td> <td class="muted">Programming and development</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Art</strong><small>Art</small><a href="#evidence" class="area-provenance">View source ↗</a></td> <td class="muted">Visual assets</td> <td><span class="state s-used">AI use disclosed</span></td> <td class="muted">The disclosure names two separate uses inside art production, image creation and image enhancement, so generative AI both produced and retouched the artwork according to the developer.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Music &amp; sound</strong><small>Music &amp; SFX</small></td> <td class="muted">Music and sound</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Voice</strong><small>Voice</small></td> <td class="muted">Voice and dialogue audio</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Writing</strong><small>Writing</small></td> <td class="muted">Story and written content</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Translation</strong><small>Translation</small><a href="#evidence" class="area-provenance">View source ↗</a></td> <td class="muted">Translation and localization</td> <td><span class="state s-used">AI use disclosed</span></td> <td class="muted">The second sentence states that generative AI was used to translate the localised content of the game.</td> </tr><tr> <td><strong>Marketing</strong><small>Marketing</small></td> <td class="muted">Promotional material</td> <td><span class="state s-not_stated">Not stated</span></td> <td class="muted">This area is not addressed by the reviewed disclosure; that is not proof of non-use.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> </div> <div class="legend"> <span><i class="dot used"></i>Reported use (official / third-party)</span> <span><i class="dot not_stated"></i>Not stated (not proof of no use)</span> <span><i class="dot claimed_none"></i>Developer claims no AI</span> <span><i class="dot unreviewed"></i>Unreviewed</span> </div> <blockquote class="quote"> <p>“Generative AI was used in the game&#39;s art production for image creation and image enhancement. Generative AI was used to translate the game&#39;s localized content.”</p> <footer>Steam 商店 AI 生成内容披露栏完整原文，2026-11-04 核查；可能随商店页更新。 · <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4958460/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read original ↗</a></footer> </blockquote> <details class="callout"> <summary><strong>How to interpret these statuses</strong></summary> <p>Reported AI use: 2/8. Developer no-use claims: 0/8. Claims are not independent verification; not stated does not mean no AI use.</p> </details> <p class="source-line"> Primary source:<a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4958460/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Official disclosure ↗</a> <span> · Reviewed 2026-11-04</span> </p> </section> <section class="section" id="evidence"> <div class="section-head"> <div><div class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE</div><h2>Evidence</h2></div> <div class="section-meta">6 sources</div> </div> <div class="timeline"> <article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Official disclosure</span> <time>2026-11-04</time> </div> <h3>Steam 商店完整 AI 披露</h3> <p>Generative AI was used in the game&#39;s art production for image creation and image enhancement. Generative AI was used to translate the game&#39;s localized content.</p> <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4958460/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Steam discussion index</span> <time>2026-11-04</time> </div> <h3>Steam 讨论区首页核查</h3> <p>英文讨论区首页显示 15 个主题（总数 15）；仅覆盖首页。</p> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/4958460/discussions/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Community report</span> <time>2026-11-04</time> </div> <h3>Please remove AI from this game, you don&#39;t understand the damage it does</h3> <p>Game looks interesting, and gameplay overall is good albeit a bit.. shallow. At least at this demo stage. But my god the traces of AI are disgusting, please don&#39;t let it ruin your game! Gray View Profile View Posts 2 Oct 21 @ 1:45pm Report this post Whole game is basically AI, with thousands of independent Touhou content artists out there, there&#39;s no real need for AI. Like, I get it if you needed a placeholder, but now that the dev has a working demo, maybe it&#39;s time to hire some small artists? Last edited by Gray ; Oct 21 @ 1:45pm #1 EskiNott View Profile View Posts [developer] 1 Oct 25 @ 1:25am Report this post I&#39;m developing this game entirely on my own, and unfortunately, my financial situation isn&#39;t great. I simply can&#39;t afford to commission artists or purchase more professional art assets. Using AI-generated artwork was a compromise I had to make due to these limitations, rather than something I would have chosen under ideal circumstances. #2 Ryon ♡ View Profile View Posts Oct 25 @ 2:57am Report this post Originally posted by EskiNott : I&#39;m developing this game entirely on my own, and unfortunately, my financial situation isn&#39;t great. I simply can&#39;t afford to commission artists or purchase more professional art assets. Using AI-generated artwork was a compromise I had to make due to these limitations, rather than something I would have chosen under ideal circumstances. In the event that you do get the money for it, will the AI artwork eventually be replaced? Because for me personally, Touhou is a franchise that thrives BECAUSE of human made art and especially music, would be a shame if this wasn’t the status quo #3 EskiNott View Profile View Posts [developer] Oct 25 @ 5:51am Report this post Originally posted by Ryon ♡ : Originally posted by EskiNott : I&#39;m developing this game entirely on my own, and unfortunately, my financial situation isn&#39;t great. I simply can&#39;t afford to commission artists or purchase more professional art assets. Using AI-generated artwork was a compromise I had to make due to these limitations, rather than something I would have chosen under ideal circumstances. In the event that you do get the money for it, will the AI artwork eventually be replaced? Because for me personally, Touhou is a franchise that thrives BECAUSE of human made art and especially music, would be a shame if this wasn’t the status quo I&#39;d certainly consider replacing the AI artwork with commissioned art if the game ends up being successful enough! However, given my current financial situation and the uncertainty of how well the game will sell, it&#39;s difficult for me to make any promises right now. #4 Haar View Profile View Posts 2 Oct 25 @ 9:07am Report this post Originally posted by EskiNott : Originally posted by Ryon ♡ : In the event that you do get the money for it, will the AI artwork eventually be replaced? Because for me personally, Touhou is a franchise that thrives BECAUSE of human made art and especially music, would be a shame if this wasn’t the status quo I&#39;d certainly consider replacing the AI artwork with commissioned art if the game ends up being successful enough! However, given my current financial situation and the uncertainty of how well the game will sell, it&#39;s difficult for me to make any promises right now. I would be much more willing to purchase the game if it wasn&#39;t AI. As it stands, it has killed my interest. Sorry. #5 Matex View Profile View Posts 1 Oct 25 @ 5:48pm Report this post i dont really care for AI at all so long as the game is fun, it lets devs cover skillsets they dont have. clear difference between copy paste slop trying to make money and a game someone wants to make. besides, there is a refund period to try games out anyway. #6 Alice View Profile View Posts Oct 26 @ 3:16am Report this post Originally posted by EskiNott : I&#39;m developing this game entirely on my own, and unfortunately, my financial situation isn&#39;t great. I simply can&#39;t afford to commission artists or purchase more professional art assets. Using AI-generated artwork was a compromise I had to make due to these limitations, rather than something I would have chosen under ideal circumstances. People will never understand this, they don&#39;t have empathy, they just want to be part of the anti-ai bubble, ignoring how helpful ai is. It&#39;s helping you to make your dream come true, but they won&#39;t understand it, they think everybody has the money to hire artists to make art and music, they think devs don&#39;t have a life or family, they live in a bubble. #7 V&#39;ehxness View Profile View Posts Oct 26 @ 8:44am Report this post &quot;Please remove AI from this game, you don&#39;t understand the damage it does&quot; People like the OP are doing the most damage by making a big deal out of nothing. Originally posted by Matex : i dont really care for AI at all so long as the game is fun... Also this. Last edited by V&#39;ehxness ; Oct 26 @ 8:44am #8 EskiNott View Profile View Posts [developer] Oct 26 @ 9:06am Report this post Originally posted by Alice : Originally posted by EskiNott : I&#39;m developing this game entirely on my own, and unfortunately, my financial situation isn&#39;t great. I simply can&#39;t afford to commission artists or purchase more professional art assets. Using AI-generated artwork was a compromise I had to make due to these limitations, rather than something I would have chosen under ideal circumstances. People will never understand this, they don&#39;t have empathy, they just want to be part of the anti-ai bubble, ignoring how helpful ai is. It&#39;s helping you to make your dream come true, but they won&#39;t understand it, they think everybody has the money to hire artists to make art and music, they think devs don&#39;t have a life or family, they live in a bubble. Thank you so much for speaking up for me! ❤️ That said, I can also understand and respect how those players feel. I know that AI-generated artwork isn&#39;t something everyone is comfortable with, and I recognize that having to rely on AI is also a reflection of my own limitations as a creator. I still have a lot to learn, and I&#39;ll keep working hard to improve my own artistic skills so that I can create more things with my own hands in the future. Thank you again for your kindness and support. ❤️ #9 楚祺 View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 11:08am Report this post I really don&#39;t understand this. First of all, this game has been carefully crafted. The developer loves Touhou and wants to bring more exciting gameplay to this IP. Even though AI was used, it&#39;s not some cheaply slapped-together, low-quality cash grab; he has put a lot of hard work into it. Nitpicking about the AI is completely meaningless. Not every game has a well-known team or publisher behind it, and not every game has sufficient funding. The developer is a solo creator who managed to complete all of this entirely on his own, which is already quite admirable. Moreover, his financial situation is poor, and he can&#39;t afford to hire an art team. Using AI was not a wrong decision. We should encourage and support him. And if the game sells well later on, he will definitely change this situation. Touhou should be an inclusive IP, shouldn&#39;t it? #10 Newby24 View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 11:22am Report this post Originally posted by 楚祺 : I really don&#39;t understand this. First of all, this game has been carefully crafted. The developer loves Touhou and wants to bring more exciting gameplay to this IP. Even though AI was used, it&#39;s not some cheaply slapped-together, low-quality cash grab; he has put a lot of hard work into it. Nitpicking about the AI is completely meaningless. Not every game has a well-known team or publisher behind it, and not every game has sufficient funding. The developer is a solo creator who managed to complete all of this entirely on his own, which is already quite admirable. Moreover, his financial situation is poor, and he can&#39;t afford to hire an art team. Using AI was not a wrong decision. We should encourage and support him. And if the game sells well later on, he will definitely change this situation. Touhou should be an inclusive IP, shouldn&#39;t it? I couldn&#39;t have said it better myself. The game doesn&#39;t really feel like AI slop and it is obvious the dev put a lot of time and care into it. Really, it is the devs that just release quick slop cashcrab for money that should be riddiculed not endeavors like this. Plus the dev already said they would like to develop art skills in the future so they can do art in their own personal artstyle without AI. With that attitude, I have no problem supporting this endeavor. #11 楚祺 View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 11:38am Report this post Originally posted by Newby24 : Originally posted by 楚祺 : I really don&#39;t understand this. First of all, this game has been carefully crafted. The developer loves Touhou and wants to bring more exciting gameplay to this IP. Even though AI was used, it&#39;s not some cheaply slapped-together, low-quality cash grab; he has put a lot of hard work into it. Nitpicking about the AI is completely meaningless. Not every game has a well-known team or publisher behind it, and not every game has sufficient funding. The developer is a solo creator who managed to complete all of this entirely on his own, which is already quite admirable. Moreover, his financial situation is poor, and he can&#39;t afford to hire an art team. Using AI was not a wrong decision. We should encourage and support him. And if the game sells well later on, he will definitely change this situation. Touhou should be an inclusive IP, shouldn&#39;t it? I couldn&#39;t have said it better myself. The game doesn&#39;t really feel like AI slop and it is obvious the dev put a lot of time and care into it. Really, it is the devs that just release quick slop cashcrab for money that should be riddiculed not endeavors like this. Plus the dev already said they would like to develop art skills in the future so they can do art in their own personal artstyle without AI. With that attitude, I have no problem supporting this endeavor. Yes, times are progressing, and AI has given many outstanding individual creators opportunities. Thanks to the development of AI, we are able to see creators one after another realizing their dreams. Many people probably haven&#39;t even seriously played this game; they take a few glances at it, label it as &#39;AI garbage,&#39; and start trashing it loudly. This is disrespectful and highly irresponsible behavior toward the developer. I&#39;ve talked with the author. He poured his heart and soul into this game and tried his best to make it as good as possible. Doing this well on a first release is already great. There always needs to be someone to speak up for fairness. Objective reviews and reasonable suggestions are completely fine, but indiscriminate criticism is truly detestable. Furthermore, the original creator of Touhou, ZUN strongly supports derivative works and encourages creators to realize their own vision of Gensokyo. This is exactly the meaning behind why the Touhou IP has been able to endure and continue to this day. #12 Newby24 View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 11:46am Report this post Originally posted by 楚祺 : Originally posted by Newby24 : I couldn&#39;t have said it better myself. The game doesn&#39;t really feel like AI slop and it is obvious the dev put a lot of time and care into it. Really, it is the devs that just release quick slop cashcrab for money that should be riddiculed not endeavors like this. Plus the dev already said they would like to develop art skills in the future so they can do art in their own personal artstyle without AI. With that attitude, I have no problem supporting this endeavor. Yes, times are progressing, and AI has given many outstanding individual creators opportunities. Thanks to the development of AI, we are able to see creators one after another realizing their dreams. Many people probably haven&#39;t even seriously played this game; they take a few glances at it, label it as &#39;AI garbage,&#39; and start trashing it loudly. This is disrespectful and highly irresponsible behavior toward the developer. I&#39;ve talked with the author. He poured his heart and soul into this game and tried his best to make it as good as possible. Doing this well on a first release is already great. There always needs to be someone to speak up for fairness. Objective reviews and reasonable suggestions are completely fine, but indiscriminate criticism is truly detestable. Furthermore, the original creator of Touhou, ZUN strongly supports derivative works and encourages creators to realize their own vision of Gensokyo. This is exactly the meaning behind why the Touhou IP has been able to endure and continue to this day. Exactly. I personally have only issue with exploitative and harmful usage of AI, be it with companies that push for data centers and crashing the economy, and for people who use it to generate slop to make a quick cash grab or plagiarize on hard working artists. ZUN himself used AI art in one of the mainline Touhou games, for the backgrounds, IIRC, and while I am raising an eyebrow on it and find it very questionable, since ZUN can draw himself very well, it was his decision. Without him and his approval we would not even have fangames like this. Personally, while I am against AI exploitation, there are good usages of AI, such as this one, that I have no problem with. Though I am in full support of human artists and their endeavors. I wouldn&#39;t have got this game if I could not see how carefuly it was crafted and that the developer really meant well. Last edited by Newby24 ; Oct 27 @ 11:47am #13 Shrimp Simp View Profile View Posts Oct 29 @ 7:38am Report this post Originally posted by EskiNott : I&#39;m developing this game entirely on my own, and unfortunately, my financial situation isn&#39;t great. I simply can&#39;t afford to commission artists or purchase more professional art assets. Using AI-generated artwork was a compromise I had to make due to these limitations, rather than something I would have chosen under ideal circumstances. Draw them yourself then, like a real man would, coward. #14 EskiNott View Profile View Posts [developer] Oct 29 @ 11:15am Report this post Originally posted by Shrimp Simp : Originally posted by EskiNott : I&#39;m developing this game entirely on my own, and unfortunately, my financial situation isn&#39;t great. I simply can&#39;t afford to commission artists or purchase more professional art assets. Using AI-generated artwork was a compromise I had to make due to these limitations, rather than something I would have chosen under ideal circumstances. Draw them yourself then, like a real man would, coward. I dont know how to draw #15</p> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/4958460/discussions/0/592943924842238700/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Community report</span> <time>2026-11-04</time> </div> <h3>Question for dev, about the extend of the AI art usage</h3> <p>While I am not pleased entirely with the AI art usage, I do understand the circumstances. As a beginner artist myself, I am slightly disappointed in that that, since there are some elements, particularly CGs, which I found really good looking, beautiful even . Were different AI models used for the art production? Because I particularly found strange that the art is very presentable and it does not at least at first glance anyway, have the usual trappings of AI image generation. I had been enjoying the game, so I am not here to throw unnecessary hate, I just want more information in regards to this. Though it is obvious, thanks to elements being different in artstyle visually, AI was used. I am rather critical of this, no matter the game, because visual incohesion is something I am able to notice and in some cases, it can actually hinder my enjoyment of a particular title. I also had seen the comments and I think it is admirable that the dev is going to work on their artistic skills so they can avod this in the future. Again, as someone who is learning how to draw, I am in full support of this decision. Thank you very much for the answer! P.S. I got this game as soon as it released, thank you for such an amazing game! It is hard for me to put down! EskiNott View Profile View Posts [developer] Oct 27 @ 10:58am Report this post No, all the artwork was created using the same AI model. However, since the development period was quite long and I’m still a beginner in this area, my art workflow changed significantly throughout development. That’s why some assets have noticeable differences in art style. Thank you so much for your understanding and support! I really appreciate it! #1 Newby24 View Profile View Posts Oct 27 @ 11:05am Report this post Originally posted by EskiNott : No, all the artwork was created using the same AI model. However, since the development period was quite long and I’m still a beginner in this area, my art workflow changed significantly throughout development. That’s why some assets have noticeable differences in art style. Thank you so much for your understanding and support! I really appreciate it! No problem. I had been anticipating this game&#39;s release ever since I discovered it and not that it finally released, I wish I could stop time, just like Sakuya, so I didn&#39;t have to worry about how much I am playing. The concept and execution are great and it is something I greatly appreciate! Thank you very much. I got the OST too, some great tunes and I figured I could support a solo developer, who clearly has passion for the Touhou series! #2 EskiNott View Profile View Posts [developer] Oct 27 @ 11:10am Report this post Originally posted by Newby24 : Originally posted by EskiNott : No, all the artwork was created using the same AI model. However, since the development period was quite long and I’m still a beginner in this area, my art workflow changed significantly throughout development. That’s why some assets have noticeable differences in art style. Thank you so much for your understanding and support! I really appreciate it! No problem. I had been anticipating this game&#39;s release ever since I discovered it and not that it finally released, I wish I could stop time, just like Sakuya, so I didn&#39;t have to worry about how much I am playing. The concept and execution are great and it is something I greatly appreciate! Thank you very much. I got the OST too, some great tunes and I figured I could support a solo developer, who clearly has passion for the Touhou series! Thank you so much！ #3</p> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/4958460/discussions/0/569301416225588091/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Third-party source</span> <time>2026-11-04</time> </div> <h3>GenPlay.gg 对该作 Steam 披露的复核页</h3> <p>Generative AI was used in the game&#39;s art production for image creation and image enhancement. Generative AI was used to translate the game&#39;s localized content.</p> <a href="https://genplay.gg/games/touhou-bansho-cards/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article><article class="evidence-card"> <div class="evidence-top"> <span class="evidence-type">Third-party source</span> <time>2026-11-04</time> </div> <h3>AI Transparency Index 该作条目（结构化数据逐字收录披露）</h3> <p>Generative AI was used in the game&#39;s art production for image creation and image enhancement.\nGenerative AI was used to translate the game&#39;s localized content.</p> <a href="https://aitransparencyindex.com/products/steam/4958460" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original source ↗</a> </article> </div> <details class="callout"><summary><strong>Review notes (expand)</strong></summary><p>Checked the complete English Steam AI disclosure, the identity (EskiNott Game Studio is both developer and publisher) and the English discussion homepage (15 visible topics of 15, so the homepage covers every topic), and read both keyword-matched threads in full including every visible reply. In Please remove AI from this game players criticise the visible AI traces and the developer answers under a developer badge that the game is made entirely alone, that their financial situation does not allow commissioning artists or buying better art assets, that AI-generated artwork was a compromise under those limits, and that replacement would be considered if sales allow. In Question for dev, about the extend of the AI art usage players ask which models were used. These are community posts and developer forum statements, recorded here as what those people said rather than as independent verification, and they do not extend any area the disclosure leaves open. This title was searched once, that one response holds 6 results and 2 raw sources were read: the genplay.gg entry and the AI Transparency Index entry both transcribe the store disclosure verbatim. The index page additionally marks the process as AI-generated and live AI during play as No with a model-reported confidence of 95 percent, while stating on the same page that this is auto-classified model output, not an accuracy rate or a human review score, and that the raw disclosure remains the source of truth; this site therefore does not adopt its live-generation finding and keeps that area unaddressed. The remaining 4 results were the store page and a curators-parameter variant of it, a storefront mirror on pcgame.com and a listing page of a deckbuilder subreddit; none carries verifiable information beyond the disclosure, so none is registered as a source.</p></details> </section> <section class="section" id="steam"> <div class="section-head"> <div><div class="eyebrow">STEAM DATA</div><h2>Steam data</h2></div> <div class="section-meta">Public data snapshot</div> </div> <div class="stat-grid"> <div class="stat"> <span>Online now</span> <strong>13</strong> <small>Steam public API</small> </div> <div class="stat"> <span>Steam reviews</span> <strong>—</strong> <small>No data</small> </div> <div class="stat"> <span>Positive reviews</span> <strong>—</strong> <small>All languages</small> </div> <div class="stat"> <span>Release date</span> <strong>2026</strong> <small>26 Oct, 2026</small> </div> </div> <div class="steam-desc"><h3>Steam description</h3><p>将战斗贯彻到底！既然已经出牌，就没有停手的理由。一次接着一次，把“连击”推得更高。让伤害越过界限，直到挡在面前的敌人被一口气轰穿！《东方万象牌》是一款 Roguelike 卡牌游戏。探索「万象牌廊」，在不同选择中把牌组推向更凶狠的方向。击败盘踞其中的残影，营救被卷入异变的少女，逐步揭开异变的真相。</p></div> <p class="source-line"> Player and review figures are Steam snapshots taken at build time and may be delayed. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4958460/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View current data on Steam ↗</a> </p> </section> <section class="section" id="developer"> <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">DEVELOPER</div><h2>Developer</h2></div></div> <div class="dev-card"> <div class="dev-avatar">ES</div> <div class="dev-body"> <h3>EskiNott Game Studio</h3> <p>Developer / publisher</p> <div class="dev-links">  <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/search/?developer=EskiNott%20Game%20Studio" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Developer on Steam ↗</a> <a href="https://github.com/COLDDCC/GameAIchecker/issues/new?title=Touhou%20Bansho%20Cards%EF%BC%884958460%EF%BC%89%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%E7%BA%A0%E9%94%99&body=%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%EF%BC%9Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fgameaichecker.com%2Fgames%2F4958460-touhou-bansho-cards%2F%0A%0A%E9%9C%80%E8%A6%81%E7%BA%A0%E6%AD%A3%E7%9A%84%E5%86%85%E5%AE%B9%EF%BC%9A%0A%0A%E5%8E%9F%E5%A7%8B%E6%9D%A5%E6%BA%90%EF%BC%9A%0A%0A%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%9F%EF%BC%9A%0A" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claim / correct ↗</a> </div> </div> </div>  </section> <section class="section" id="community"> <div class="section-head"> <div><div class="eyebrow">COMMUNITY</div><h2>Player impressions</h2></div> <div class="section-meta">Separate from official disclosures</div> </div> <p class="section-lede">Player impressions are not evidence of AI use. Votes do not change developer disclosure findings.</p> <form id="voteForm" class="vote-form"> <select id="voteSelect" required aria-label="Choose your impression"> <option value="">Your impression…</option> <option value="no_ai_suspected">I suspect no AI use</option> <option value="some_ai_suspected">I suspect some AI use</option> <option value="heavy_ai_suspected">I suspect extensive AI use</option> <option value="all_ai_suspected">I suspect AI throughout</option> </select> <button class="btn primary" type="submit">Submit</button> </form> <p id="voteMessage" class="muted" role="status"></p> <div id="voteCounts" class="vote-counts"></div> <p class="source-line">Feedback availability does not affect the evidence. One vote per network per game.</p> </section> <section class="section" id="sources"> <div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">SOURCES</div><h2>Sources &amp; review limits</h2></div></div> <ul class="source-list"> <li> <span>Official disclosure</span> <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4958460/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Steam 商店完整 AI 披露</a> <time>2026-11-04</time> </li><li> <span>Steam discussion index</span> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/4958460/discussions/?l=english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Steam 讨论区首页核查</a> <time>2026-11-04</time> </li><li> <span>Community report</span> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/4958460/discussions/0/592943924842238700/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Please remove AI from this game, you don&#39;t understand the damage it does</a> <time>2026-11-04</time> </li><li> <span>Community report</span> <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/4958460/discussions/0/569301416225588091/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Question for dev, about the extend of the AI art usage</a> <time>2026-11-04</time> </li><li> <span>Third-party source</span> <a href="https://genplay.gg/games/touhou-bansho-cards/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GenPlay.gg 对该作 Steam 披露的复核页</a> <time>2026-11-04</time> </li><li> <span>Third-party source</span> <a href="https://aitransparencyindex.com/products/steam/4958460" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Transparency Index 该作条目（结构化数据逐字收录披露）</a> <time>2026-11-04</time> </li> <li> <span>Steam store</span> <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4958460/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Touhou Bansho Cards · App 4958460</a> <time></time> </li> </ul> <div class="callout"> <strong>Found an error?</strong> <p> Please include an original source, date and specific correction. <a href="https://github.com/COLDDCC/GameAIchecker/issues/new?title=Touhou%20Bansho%20Cards%EF%BC%884958460%EF%BC%89%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%E7%BA%A0%E9%94%99&body=%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%EF%BC%9Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fgameaichecker.com%2Fgames%2F4958460-touhou-bansho-cards%2F%0A%0A%E9%9C%80%E8%A6%81%E7%BA%A0%E6%AD%A3%E7%9A%84%E5%86%85%E5%AE%B9%EF%BC%9A%0A%0A%E5%8E%9F%E5%A7%8B%E6%9D%A5%E6%BA%90%EF%BC%9A%0A%0A%E6%97%A5%E6%9C%9F%EF%BC%9A%0A" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Suggest a correction ↗</a> or <a href="https://github.com/COLDDCC/GameAIchecker/issues/new?title=Touhou%20Bansho%20Cards%20%E9%A1%B5%E9%9D%A2%E7%BA%A0%E9%94%99" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open a GitHub issue ↗</a>。
</p> </div> </section> <div class="share-bar"> <span>Share this game</span> <button class="btn" id="shareBtn2" type="button">Copy link</button> <a class="btn" href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=Does%20Touhou%20Bansho%20Cards%20use%20AI%3F&url=https%3A%2F%2Fgameaichecker.com%2Fgames%2F4958460-touhou-bansho-cards%2F" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Share on X</a> <a class="btn" href="https://www.reddit.com/submit?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgameaichecker.com%2Fgames%2F4958460-touhou-bansho-cards%2F&title=Touhou%20Bansho%20Cards%20%E2%80%94%20AI%20use%20evidence" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Reddit</a> </div> </main> <div class="tf-cta-wrap"><a class="tf-cta" href="https://toolfavor.com/?utm_source=gameaichecker&utm_medium=footer_button" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3l1.9 4.6L18.5 9.5l-4.6 1.9L12 16l-1.9-4.6L5.5 9.5l4.6-1.9z"></path><path d="M19 15l.8 1.9 1.9.8-1.9.8L19 20.4l-.8-1.9-1.9-.8 1.9-.8z"></path></svg><span>Discover more useful tools on ToolFavor</span><svg class="tf-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></a></div> <footer class="site-footer"> <div class="wrap"> <span>Game AI Checker · Independent of Valve / Steam.</span> <span>Evidence first · Not stated does not mean unused</span> </div> </footer> <dialog class="lightbox" id="lightbox"> <button id="closeLightbox" type="button" aria-label="Close">×</button> <img id="lightboxImg" alt="" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high"> <div class="lightbox-caption" id="lightboxCaption"></div> </dialog> <script>
    (() => {
      const app = document.getElementById('app');
      const labels = JSON.parse(app?.dataset.ui || '{}');
      const tx = key => labels[key] || key;
      const en = document.documentElement.lang === 'en';
      const key = app?.dataset.gameKey || '';
      const slug = app?.dataset.slug || '';

      document.querySelectorAll('img[data-fallback]').forEach((img) => {
        const fallback = img.dataset.fallback;
        if (!fallback) return;
        img.addEventListener('error', function onError() {
          img.removeEventListener('error', onError);
          img.dataset.fallback = '';
          img.src = fallback;
          img.addEventListener('error', () => { img.style.display = 'none'; }, { once: true });
        });
      });

      const heroImg = document.getElementById('heroImg');
      const heroMedia = document.getElementById('heroMedia');
      const thumbs = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.thumb'));
      const counter = document.getElementById('mediaCount');
      const pauseBtn = document.getElementById('pauseBtn');
      let index = 0;
      let paused = false;
      let hovering = false;
      let timer = null;

      const warmedImages = new Set();
      function warm(full) {
        if (!full || warmedImages.has(full)) return null;
        warmedImages.add(full);
        const image = new Image();
        image.decoding = 'async';
        image.src = full;
        return image;
      }
      // Browse one frame ahead so the lightbox never waits on a cold round trip.
      function warmAround() {
        if (!thumbs.length) return;
        const upcoming = [thumbs[index], thumbs[(index + 1) % thumbs.length]];
        const run = () => upcoming.forEach((thumb) => thumb && warm(thumb.dataset.full));
        if (typeof window.requestIdleCallback === 'function') window.requestIdleCallback(run, { timeout: 1500 });
        else setTimeout(run, 500);
      }

      function show(next) {
        if (!heroImg || !thumbs.length) return;
        index = (next + thumbs.length) % thumbs.length;
        const thumb = thumbs[index];
        heroImg.src = thumb.dataset.src || heroImg.src;
        heroImg.dataset.full = thumb.dataset.full || heroImg.dataset.full;
        thumbs.forEach((item, position) => item.classList.toggle('active', position === index));
        if (counter) counter.textContent = `${index + 1} / ${thumbs.length}`;
        warmAround();
      }

      function schedule() {
        clearInterval(timer);
        if (thumbs.length < 2 || paused || hovering || document.hidden) return;
        timer = setInterval(() => show(index + 1), 6000);
      }

      thumbs.forEach((thumb) => {
        thumb.addEventListener('click', () => {
          show(Number(thumb.dataset.index || 0));
          schedule();
        });
      });

      document.getElementById('prevBtn')?.addEventListener('click', () => { show(index - 1); schedule(); });
      document.getElementById('nextBtn')?.addEventListener('click', () => { show(index + 1); schedule(); });
      pauseBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        paused = !paused;
        pauseBtn.textContent = paused ? '▶' : 'Ⅱ';
        pauseBtn.setAttribute('aria-label', paused ? tx("继续轮播") : tx("暂停轮播"));
        schedule();
      });
      heroMedia?.addEventListener('mouseenter', () => { hovering = true; schedule(); });
      heroMedia?.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => { hovering = false; schedule(); });
      document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', schedule);
      schedule();

      const appId = app?.dataset.appid;
      if (appId && heroImg && !heroImg.getAttribute('src')?.startsWith('/images/steam/')) {
        fetch(`/api/steam-media?id=${encodeURIComponent(appId)}`)
          .then((response) => (response.ok ? response.json() : Promise.reject()))
          .then((data) => {
            if (!data?.available) return;
            for (const shot of data.screenshots || []) {
              const src = shot.thumbnail || shot.full;
              const full = shot.full || shot.thumbnail;
              if (!src || thumbs.some((thumb) => thumb.dataset.full === full)) continue;
              const thumb = document.createElement('button');
              thumb.className = 'thumb';
              thumb.type = 'button';
              thumb.dataset.src = src;
              thumb.dataset.full = full;
              thumb.dataset.index = String(thumbs.length);
              thumb.setAttribute('aria-label', `第 ${thumbs.length + 1} 张图片`);
              const image = document.createElement('img');
              image.src = src;
              image.alt = '';
              image.loading = 'lazy';
              image.decoding = 'async';
              thumb.append(image);
              thumb.addEventListener('click', () => { show(Number(thumb.dataset.index)); schedule(); });
              document.getElementById('thumbs')?.append(thumb);
              thumbs.push(thumb);
            }
            if (counter) counter.textContent = `${index + 1} / ${thumbs.length}`;
            const countText = document.getElementById('mediaCountText');
            if (countText) countText.textContent = `${thumbs.length} ${en ? 'official images' : '张官方图片'}`;
            schedule();

            if (data.movies?.length) {
              const mediaCol = document.querySelector('.media-col');
              let videos = document.querySelector('.videos');
              if (!videos && mediaCol) {
                videos = document.createElement('div');
                videos.className = 'videos';
                videos.innerHTML = '<div class="mini-title"></div><div class="video-grid"></div>';
                videos.querySelector('.mini-title').textContent = tx('宣传视频');
                mediaCol.append(videos);
              }
              const grid = videos?.querySelector('.video-grid');
              if (grid) {
                const first = data.movies.find((movie) => movie.webm || movie.mp4);
                if (first) {
                  const player = document.createElement('video');
                  player.className = 'trailer';
                  player.controls = true;
                  player.preload = 'none';
                  player.poster = first.thumbnail || '';
                  player.src = first.webm || first.mp4;
                  grid.before(player);
                }
                for (const movie of data.movies.slice(0, 4)) {
                  if (!movie.thumbnail) continue;
                  const link = document.createElement('a');
                  link.className = 'video-card';
                  link.href = data.steamUrl || `https://store.steampowered.com/app/${appId}/`;
                  link.target = '_blank';
                  link.rel = 'noopener noreferrer';
                  const poster = document.createElement('img');
                  poster.src = movie.thumbnail;
                  poster.alt = movie.name || tx("宣传视频");
                  poster.loading = 'lazy';
                  const label = document.createElement('span');
                  label.textContent = `${movie.name || tx("观看宣传视频")} ↗`;
                  link.append(poster, label);
                  grid.append(link);
                }
              }
            }
          })
          .catch(() => {});
      }

      const lightbox = document.getElementById('lightbox');
      const lightboxImg = document.getElementById('lightboxImg');
      const lightboxCaption = document.getElementById('lightboxCaption');
      function openLightbox() {
        if (!heroImg || !lightbox || !lightboxImg) return;
        const full = heroImg.dataset.full || heroImg.src;
        // The 1280 hero frame is already decoded, so the dialog shows at once and upgrades in place.
        lightboxImg.src = heroImg.currentSrc || heroImg.src;
        lightboxImg.alt = heroImg.alt || '';
        if (lightboxCaption) lightboxCaption.textContent = heroImg.alt || '';
        if (typeof lightbox.showModal === 'function') lightbox.showModal();
        const larger = warm(full);
        if (larger) larger.onload = () => { lightboxImg.src = larger.src; };
      }
      document.getElementById('openLightbox')?.addEventListener('click', openLightbox);
      heroImg?.addEventListener('click', openLightbox);
      [document.getElementById('openLightbox'), heroMedia].forEach((node) => node?.addEventListener('pointerenter', () => warm(heroImg?.dataset.full), { once: true }));
      document.getElementById('closeLightbox')?.addEventListener('click', () => lightbox?.close());
      lightbox?.addEventListener('click', (event) => { if (event.target === lightbox) lightbox.close(); });

      const saveBtn = document.getElementById('saveBtn');
      const starKey = `gac:star:${slug}`;
      function paintStar() {
        if (!saveBtn) return;
        const active = localStorage.getItem(starKey) === '1';
        saveBtn.textContent = active ? tx("★ 已收藏") : tx("☆ 收藏");
        saveBtn.classList.toggle('active', active);
      }
      saveBtn?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (localStorage.getItem(starKey) === '1') localStorage.removeItem(starKey);
        else localStorage.setItem(starKey, '1');
        paintStar();
      });
      paintStar();

      async function copyLink() {
        const url = window.location.href;
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(url);
          flash(tx("链接已复制"));
        } catch {
          window.prompt(tx("复制链接"), url);
        }
      }
      function flash(message) {
        const target = document.getElementById('voteMessage') || document.getElementById('shareBtn');
        if (!target) return;
        const original = target.textContent;
        if (target.id === 'voteMessage') {
          target.textContent = message;
          setTimeout(() => { target.textContent = original; }, 2200);
        } else {
          target.textContent = message;
          setTimeout(() => { target.textContent = tx("分享"); }, 2200);
        }
      }
      async function share() {
        if (navigator.share) {
          try {
            await navigator.share({ title: document.title, url: window.location.href });
            return;
          } catch {}
        }
        copyLink();
      }
      document.getElementById('shareBtn')?.addEventListener('click', share);
      document.getElementById('shareBtn2')?.addEventListener('click', copyLink);

      document.getElementById('copyId')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        const id = app?.dataset.appid;
        if (!id) return;
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(id);
          flash(tx("App ID 已复制"));
        } catch {}
      });

      const voteForm = document.getElementById('voteForm');
      const voteMessage = document.getElementById('voteMessage');
      const voteCounts = document.getElementById('voteCounts');
      const voteSelect = document.getElementById('voteSelect');
      const voteNames = {
        no_ai_suspected: tx("认为没有使用 AI"),
        some_ai_suspected: tx("认为部分使用 AI"),
        heavy_ai_suspected: tx("认为大量使用 AI"),
        all_ai_suspected: tx("认为几乎全程使用 AI"),
      };
      function showCounts(counts) {
        if (!voteCounts) return;
        voteCounts.replaceChildren();
        for (const [code, label] of Object.entries(voteNames)) {
          const value = Number(counts?.[code] || 0);
          if (!value) continue;
          const row = document.createElement('div');
          row.textContent = en ? `${value} players ${label}` : `${value} 位玩家${label}`;
          voteCounts.append(row);
        }
      }
      if (voteForm && key) {
        fetch(`/api/feedback?game=${encodeURIComponent(key)}`)
          .then((response) => (response.ok ? response.json() : Promise.reject()))
          .then((data) => {
            showCounts(data.counts);
            if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = tx("反馈功能已启用。");
          })
          .catch(() => {
            if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = tx("匿名反馈暂未启用，等待管理员配置数据库。");
          });
        voteForm.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
          event.preventDefault();
          const vote = voteSelect?.value;
          if (!vote) return;
          const button = voteForm.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
          if (button) button.disabled = true;
          try {
            const response = await fetch('/api/feedback', {
              method: 'POST',
              headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
              body: JSON.stringify({ game: key, vote }),
            });
            const data = await response.json();
            if (!response.ok) {
              if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = response.status === 409 ? tx("该网络已对本游戏投过票。") : tx("提交失败，请稍后再试。");
              if (data.counts) showCounts(data.counts);
            } else {
              if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = tx("反馈已记录，谢谢参与。");
              showCounts(data.counts);
              voteForm.reset();
            }
          } catch {
            if (voteMessage) voteMessage.textContent = tx("网络错误，请稍后重试。");
          } finally {
            if (button) button.disabled = false;
          }
        });
      }

      const navLinks = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.section-nav a'));
      if (navLinks.length && 'IntersectionObserver' in window) {
        const linksById = new Map(navLinks.map((link) => [link.getAttribute('href')?.slice(1), link]));
        const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          for (const entry of entries) {
            if (!entry.isIntersecting) continue;
            navLinks.forEach((link) => link.classList.remove('active'));
            linksById.get(entry.target.id)?.classList.add('active');
          }
        }, { rootMargin: '-35% 0px -55% 0px' });
        document.querySelectorAll('section[id]').forEach((section) => observer.observe(section));
      }
    })();
  </script> <script>
    document.getElementById('game-language')?.addEventListener('change', (event) => {
      const slug = document.getElementById('app')?.dataset.slug;
      if (slug) window.location.assign('/games/' + (event.target.value === 'en' ? '' : event.target.value + '/') + encodeURIComponent(slug) + '/' + location.hash);
    });
  </script> </body> </html>